    {
      "id": "BCpex-lYwdpw8oR58ADdx",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 414.7089320658499,
      "y": 343.99317610182874,
      "width": 416.7414964552917,
      "height": 47.534199005341,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 492221849,
      "version": 145,
      "versionNonce": 673082937,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791191640279,
      "created": 1791191623878,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Design a Rate Limiter ",
      "fontSize": 38.02735920427279,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Design a Rate Limiter ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "fhzTYPzIY4vphZKS2xh9F",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 418.2765260592373,
      "y": 402.4248185323279,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a2",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 980550514,
      "version": 254,
      "versionNonce": 829464046,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791191953376,
      "created": 1791191944373,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A rate limiter controls how many requests a client can make within a specific\ntimeframe. It acts like a traffic controller for your API - allowing, for example,\n100 requests per minute from a user, then rejecting excess requests with an\nHTTP 429 \"Too Many Requests\" response. Rate limiters prevent abuse, protect\nyour servers from being overwhelmed by bursts of traffic, and ensure fair usage\nacross all users.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A rate limiter controls how many requests a client can make within a specific timeframe. It acts like a traffic controller for your API - allowing, for example, 100 requests per minute from a user, then rejecting excess requests with an HTTP 429 \"Too Many Requests\" response. Rate limiters prevent abuse, protect your servers from being overwhelmed by bursts of traffic, and ensure fair usage across all users.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0ToCxZ5lZyUkEDcH8d_uk",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 425.97607064182375,
      "y": 575.4812013485489,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 900,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a4",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1812596599,
      "version": 1855,
      "versionNonce": 632740862,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791197299482,
      "created": 1791192323924,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Functional Requirements\n- uniquely identify the client based of ID , IP, or API key to apply appriate limits\n- configurable rules (100 api req  per min per user )\n- when it exceeds, we ofc reject them and \"429\" Too Many Requests \n(OUT OF SCOPE)\n-Analytics\n-rate limiting data\n\n # what are we rate limiting acutally , is it something that might change the\nscope of our problem\n# intra micro services or user based application \n\nNon functional Requirements \n    -> (CAP theorem) (availability >> consistency)\n    #scale\n    -> 100 million DAU \n    -> 1 million RPS\n    -> low latency (<50ms)  ( we DONT  want to ADD additional time)\n\nCore entities\n    ->request\n    ->Client \n    ->rules\n\nSystem Interface\n\n    isReqAllowed(clientId, RulesId,RequestId) -> \n    {\n        allowed: true // (boolean)\n        requestLeft: 30 // (Integer)\n        resetTiming:  1 sec //time or //time stamp\n        \n    }\n\n \n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Functional Requirements\n- uniquely identify the client based of ID , IP, or API key to apply appriate limits\n- configurable rules (100 api req  per min per user )\n- when it exceeds, we ofc reject them and \"429\" Too Many Requests \n(OUT OF SCOPE)\n-Analytics\n-rate limiting data\n\n # what are we rate limiting acutally , is it something that might change the scope of our problem\n# intra micro services or user based application \n\nNon functional Requirements \n    -> (CAP theorem) (availability >> consistency)\n    #scale\n    -> 100 million DAU \n    -> 1 million RPS\n    -> low latency (<50ms)  ( we DONT  want to ADD additional time)\n\nCore entities\n    ->request\n    ->Client \n    ->rules\n\nSystem Interface\n\n    isReqAllowed(clientId, RulesId,RequestId) -> \n    {\n        allowed: true // (boolean)\n        requestLeft: 30 // (Integer)\n        resetTiming:  1 sec //time or //time stamp\n        \n    }\n\n \n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
